{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794289235,"nonce":"Z8tEMNW1N4H0C4BSKCKgoeK3pL0=","title":"Keys on non-US layouts type the wrong character: the text is rebuilt from a US key table (AltGr+Q gives 2, + gives =, # gives 3)","message":"On a German layout a focused TextInput receives the wrong character for every symbol key whose US position differs. AltGr+Q (the `@`) types `2`, the `+` key types `=`, the `#` key types `3`, Shift+7 (`/`) types `?`. Phone numbers (`+`) and e-mail addresses (`@`) cannot be typed.\n\nReproduction (no desktop session touched): nested `kwin_wayland --virtual` with `XKB_DEFAULT_LAYOUT=de`, a window with TextInputs, key events through `org_kde_kwin_fake_input` with evdev codes. Focused field, one key per row:\n\n    keys (evdev)         de layout should type   typed\n    AltGr (100) + 16     @                       2\n    27                   +                       =\n    43                   #                       3\n    Shift (42) + 8       /                       ?\n    Shift (42) + 10      )                       )   (correct)\n    AltGr (100) + 9      [                       [   (correct)\n    AltGr (100) + 5      1/4 (U+00BC)            1/4 (correct)\n\nThe correct rows are the characters that have no `Key` variant (they arrive as `Key::Char`).\n\nCause: two steps, both throw the real character away.\n1. extensions/blinc_platform_desktop/src/input.rs, `convert_key`: for `WinitKey::Character` the character is folded into a US key variant (`'@'` =\u003e `Key::Num2`, `'#'` =\u003e `Key::Num3`, `'+'` =\u003e `Key::Equals`, `'/'` =\u003e `Key::Slash`, ...). The comment says this is so chord tables resolve the same physical key on any layout.\n2. crates/blinc_app/src/windowed/event_loop/input/keyboard.rs, `collect_keyboard`: `key_char` is rebuilt from that `Key` with a US table (`Key::Num2 =\u003e if shift { '@' } else { '2' }`, `Key::Equals =\u003e if shift { '+' } else { '=' }`) and sent as TEXT_INPUT. With AltGr, `mods.shift` is false, so `@` becomes `2`.\n\nProposed fix: keep `Key` for shortcuts, and carry the text winit gives (`KeyEvent::text`, or the `Character` of `logical_key`) in `KeyboardEvent` as `text: Option\u003cString\u003e`. `collect_keyboard` sends that as TEXT_INPUT and uses the US table only when it is `None`. Shortcut handling does not change.\n\nFound while testing the input components of the FreeSynergy fields crate. Evidence picture and scenario: the live probe in fs-components `tools/live-probe` (scenario `scnD-keys.txt`).","files":null}]}